  [1m4. Retry Loop Without Backoff[0m

  Instant retries re-hammer a degraded service, preventing recovery (cascading collapse). Synchronized clients
  cause thundering herd—overwhelming spikes. Exponential backoff (2^attempt) stretches retries, giving recovery
  windows. Jitter desynchronizes clients. Safe to skip only on highly reliable idempotent operations, but
  backoff cost is trivial—include it anyway.

